# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. ronald_wainwright's first conversation.

~ start
set ronald_wainwright_met
Narrator: He stands by the heavy timber post like part of the framing, smelling of pipe tallow and wet wool.
ronald_wainwright [neutral]: Evening to you. Mind the step by the barrels, the wood stays slick.
* Ask about his guard work here -> about_self
* Ask what he thinks of Wickermoor Village -> about_village
* Ask about the three children downstairs -> rumour
* [Perception DC 12] Notice the worn charms on his coat -> charm_ok | charm_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
ronald_wainwright [neutral]: I am right here if you need pointing somewhere.
* Ask about his guard work here -> about_self
* Ask what he thinks of Wickermoor Village -> about_village
* Ask about the three children downstairs -> rumour
* [Perception DC 12] Notice the worn charms on his coat -> charm_ok | charm_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_self
ronald_wainwright [neutral]: Wilma tells me where to stand, and I stand there until the bell changes. Most folks behave once they see the pair of us.
-> menu

~ about_village
ronald_wainwright [neutral]: It is a quiet hollow if you leave the old trees be and honour the Green Queen. The Oak in the Round has watched over worse nights than this.
-> menu

~ rumour
ronald_wainwright [smile]: Zachariah whittled a wooden hare yesterday and Eddie tried to trade it to Mr. Tolliver for peppermints. Good lads, and Victoria keeps them in line.
-> menu

~ charm_ok
Narrator: Braided oak twine and three small wooden tokens hang inside his cuff, polished smooth by his thumb.
ronald_wainwright [weary]: One knot for each child down in the cellar, prayed over at the Founder's Round. A man cannot watch every shadow, so he asks the Queen to watch too.
-> menu

~ charm_fail
ronald_wainwright [neutral]: Just an old wool coat, friend. Keeps the moor chill off my shoulders.
-> menu
